    {
      "id": "https://wan-ifra.org/?p=122217",
      "title": "Every moment, every match: how the Guardian rewrote its reader-revenue pitch for the World Cup",
      "link": "https://wan-ifra.org/2026/10/every-moment-every-match-how-the-guardian-rewrote-its-reader-revenue-pitch-for-the-world-cup/",
      "published": "Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:13:46 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "<p>At Digital Media Europe, The Guardian's Liz Wynn discussed their 1.4m supporters, digital reader revenue at 45 percent of turnover, a podcast whose audience doubled, and why. The call to action was the app. A pitch built for one audience, a tournament full of another.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org/2026/10/every-moment-every-match-how-the-guardian-rewrote-its-reader-revenue-pitch-for-the-world-cup/\">Every moment, every match: how the Guardian rewrote its reader-revenue pitch for the World Cup</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://wan-ifra.org\">WAN-IFRA</a>.</p>",
      "source": "WAN-IFRA"
    },
