    {
      "id": "https://www.niemanlab.org/?p=254491",
      "title": "In the AI age, publishers who understand what readers want will do best, a new report argues",
      "link": "https://www.niemanlab.org/2026/10/in-the-ai-age-publishers-who-understand-what-readers-want-will-do-best-a-new-report-argues/",
      "published": "Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:23:35 +0000",
      "summary_raw": "AI inverts the traditional journalism hierarchy: Instead of reporters gathering information, editors deciding how to present it, and newsrooms releasing the same final story to everyone, AI agents deliver what readers ask for, refining or expanding on information as requested. It&#8217;s &#8220;an interactive process in a way the current news system isn’t,&#8221; write the authors...",
